.TH BYTE_RSKIP 3
.SH NAME
byte_rskip \- count the run of a byte at the end of a byte array
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <byte.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t byte_rskip(const void* " p ", size_t " n ", char " c ");
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B byte_rskip
returns the number of consecutive bytes equal to c at the end of p.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The run length; if the whole array is c, it returns n; if n is 0, it returns 0.
.PP
These are the single-byte counterparts of the scan_charset*skip functions.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR byte_skip (3),
.BR byte_rskipn (3)
